KG42.register("rules-8235ed20232f1f804f233512",{"id":"35-microgrid_pool_strategy::v141-c-R007","paper":"35-microgrid_pool_strategy","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"Local DEM clearing prices (DLMPs) provide feedback price signals for decentralized microgrid bidding/offering decisions. Scope: DLMP feedback to microgrids in the decentralized distribution electricity market pool strategy. The microgrid may autonomously make its scheduling and bidding/offering decisions in response to distribution-system operating states and market price signals. Scope: Autonomous microgrid decisions responding to distribution-system operating states and market price signals. Condition: The microgrid acts as a price-maker with an independent operator.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g02-E28"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Autonomous microgrid decisions responding to distribution-system operating states and market price signals. | DLMP feedback to microgrids in the decentralized distribution electricity market pool strategy.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g02-E28"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"x-R007-base-bid-price","symbol":"\\lambda'^{P}_{jt}","meaning":"MG base bidding/offering price in time t, set from the DLMP at the MG's distribution node b'_j; the source calls this the base bidding/offering price used by the MG.","kind":"operational","domain":"unspecified in source; price (examples reported in $/p.u.)","unit":"$/p.u.","indices":["j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E28"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta-R007-dlmp","symbol":"\\lambda^{P}_{bt}","meaning":"Real-power distribution locational marginal price (DLMP) at DS node b in time t, declared at the DS level through the DEM clearing mechanism and used as the price signal to MG bids/offers.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"DLMP declared through DEM clearing; no fixed numerical value"},"unit":"$/p.u.","indices":["b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E28"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local DEM clearing prices (DLMPs) provide feedback price signals for decentralized microgrid bidding/offering decisions. Scope: DLMP feedback to microgrids in the decentralized distribution electricity market pool strategy.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g02-E28"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The microgrid may autonomously make its scheduling and bidding/offering decisions in response to distribution-system operating states and market price signals. Scope: Autonomous microgrid decisions responding to distribution-system operating states and market price signals. Condition: The microgrid acts as a price-maker with an independent operator.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The MG uses the DLMPs generated by the DEM clearing model as its base bidding/offering price: the base bidding/offering price at MG j's distribution node equals the DLMP at that node.","expression":"\\lambda'^{P}_{jt} = \\lambda^{P}_{b'_j t}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x-R007-base-bid-price"],"parameter_refs":["theta-R007-dlmp"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E28"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E06","location":{"location_id":"src-169a788abb-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. OUTLINE AND ASSUMPTIONS","anchor_text":"y p ( ) , p ator accepts a wide range of management rules beyond the net- tak work operation of DNO ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The pool bidding [28] and the coordinated management [14] are used together to solve the problem of high penetration levels of MGs in DS. The MGs are strategic players whose bids/offers are subject to market profile, which is decided by nonstrategic players such as the DS customers, DS-owned DGs, and high voltage utility nonstrategic players. The distribution electricity market uses a price signal such as distribution locational marginal price (DLMP) as feedback to MG’s bids/offers. The DLMPs are widely used as price signals among market participants or between the market operator and the market agent [29]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E08","location":{"location_id":"src-169a788abb-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. OUTLINE AND ASSUMPTIONS","anchor_text":"on he ed x- al t- Fig. 1. Decentralized pool strategy for distributed electricity market. t- e- n- a","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The microgrid as a price-maker with an independent operator has autonomy to make its own scheduling and bidding/offering decisions in response to distribution system operation states and market price signals which leverage the MGs’ transactive capabilities in the distributed electricity market [29]. As a result, it can help the distribution system operator reduce the decision burden and network complexity."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E28","location":{"location_id":"src-169a788abb-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"D. MG Bidding/Offering Strategy","anchor_text":"ding/offering price (α jt) based on two pieces of price infor T mation: MG corresponding marginal co","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To provide a remedy to the issues, we propose a direct and simple bidding/offering strategy for microgrids to find bidding/offering price (\\alpha'_{jt}) based on two pieces of price information: MG corresponding marginal cost (\\beta_{jt}) and DLMPs (\\lambda_{bt}) in DS. The marginal cost of an MG can be obtained at the intersection of the aggregated marginal cost curve of its DGs and the maximum capacity of its PCC. DLMPs are declared at the DS level through the DEM clearing mechanism. Hence, a modified bidding/offering strategy for MGs is proposed as follows:"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-169a788abb-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"A. Bi-Level Programming Model","anchor_text":"ket. Vmin ≤Vbt ≤Vmax : πminbt , πmaxbt , ∀b ∈B, ∀t} (16) ad. ow The objective function of the upper ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The DLMPs (λPbt) are endogenously generated from the lower-level programming model (8)–(16) (LLPM), and the MG uses DLMPs as the base bidding/offering price λPb′jt. The real power and reactive power exchange at PCC belong to the feasible set defined by the LLPM as in constraint (8)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-169a788abb-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"A. Bi-Level Programming Model","anchor_text":"ket. Vmin ≤Vbt ≤Vmax : πminbt , πmaxbt , ∀b ∈B, ∀t} (16) ad. ow The objective function of the upper ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The DLMPs (\\lambda^{P}_{bt}) are endogenously generated from the lower-level programming model (8)-(16) (LLPM), and the MG uses DLMPs as the base bidding/offering price \\lambda'^{P}_{jt}. The real power and reactive power exchange at PCC belong to the feasible set defined by the LLPM as in constraint (8)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E06","quote":"The distribution electricity market uses a price signal such as distribution locational marginal price (DLMP) as feedback to MG’s bids/offers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E28","quote":"DLMPs are declared at the DS level through the DEM clearing mechanism."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E08","quote":"The microgrid as a price-maker with an independent operator has autonomy to make its own scheduling and bidding/offering decisions in response to distribution system operation states and market price signals"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"7ac05cb755ade83dcb4977359dfa244f9d383d4ef38bb3105da819e296176799","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The frozen rule graph represents the source's DLMP feedback relation by the edge pricing.local -> coordination.price_signal. The source supplies a direct supported identity for that relation: the MG uses DLMPs generated by DEM clearing as its base bidding/offering price (v141-b-g01-E11, v141-b-g02-E15, v141-b-g02-E28). I add that base-price feedback identity as C003 and declare only the two symbols needed for it. The qualitative autonomy statement in C002 remains procedural/not_formalized because it does not supply a separate equation within this rule.","bindings":[{"object_id":"x-R007-base-bid-price","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"The base bidding/offering price is the MG-side price formed in the price-signal coordination relation; the rule edge carries the DLMP feedback from pricing.local to coordination.price_signal."},{"object_id":"theta-R007-dlmp","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"The DLMP is the local DEM clearing price supplied by pricing.local and transmitted as the feedback signal along the rule edge to coordination.price_signal."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","node_ids":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"The identity equates the DLMP from local DEM pricing with the MG base bid/offer price in coordination, which is exactly the source-supported pricing.local -> coordination.price_signal relation."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
